DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       These functions return the hyperbolic sine of _x, which is defined math‐
       ematically as:

           sinh(x) = (exp(x) - exp(-x)) / 2

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, these functions return the hyperbolic sine of _x.

       If _x is a NaN, a NaN is returned.

       If _x is +0 (-0), +0 (-0) is returned.

       If _x is positive infinity (negative infinity), positive infinity (nega‐
       tive infinity) is returned.

       If the result overflows, a range error occurs, and the functions return
       HHUUGGEE__VVAALL,  HHUUGGEE__VVAALLFF, or HHUUGGEE__VVAALLLL, respectively, with the same sign as
       _x.

